    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The whole test suite consists of `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are helper base classes), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a read-only `timezone` field to the owner response, derived from the region/locality via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nTwo files touched:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `timezone` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` gets `getTimezone`/`setTimezone`.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a new, tiny `@AfterMapping` method `deriveTimezone` plus a constant `REGION_TIMEZONE` map. It reads the already-derived `locality` and looks up the IANA name.\n\nKeeping structural impact low:\n- The new logic is a fresh method with cyclomatic complexity 1 (a single map lookup), rather than growing an existing method \u2014 so it never multiplies the surrounding `WMC_other` by a higher CC or extra changed lines.\n- It reuses the `locality` already computed by `deriveLocality` (which appears earlier in source order, so MapStruct runs it first), avoiding any duplication of the customerCode/postcode region logic.\n- Unknown regions simply get no entry, leaving `timezone` unset \u2014 no extra branching.",
